  "description": "Meta's Segment Anything Model 3: it finds every object a short phrase names, such as curb ramp or traffic cone, in an image or a video, outlines each with a mask, and follows each one from frame to frame under one id. Its Track Objects node runs it on a collection's videos and writes an overlay video, which Simple View plays, and a table of one row per object. The weights, 3.4 GB and gated by Meta, are in neither the Curio repository nor the pip package: whoever runs Curio fetches them once with scripts/fetch_model_weights.py.",
